Inventory-skewed quoting adapts the normalized reservation-price and exponential
order-amount (eta) designs from Hummingbot's avellaneda_market_making strategy,
revision 9af100d6822da7d2d0291a906c730ef172284ee2, under Apache License 2.0.
Glyde uses signed perpetual position relative to equity instead of spot balances.

The fixed-range grid references Hummingbot's linearly distributed grid-level
design in strategy_v2/executors/grid_executor, revision
9af100d6822da7d2d0291a906c730ef172284ee2, under Apache License 2.0.
Glyde's simple two-sided grid is rewritten around its shared PMM lifecycle; it
does not include Hummingbot's separate executor or paired take-profit logic.

PMM directional price bands, additive ladder sizing and ping-pong design reference
Hummingbot pure_market_making, revision 9af100d6822da7d2d0291a906c730ef172284ee2,
under Apache License 2.0. Glyde rewrites the lifecycle and alternates entire sides
on identified partial paper fills rather than Hummingbot's completed-order count.

PMM inventory ratio/range, refresh tolerance and post-fill delay also reference
Hummingbot pure_market_making under Apache License 2.0. The implementation is
rewritten with Decimal and shared risk admission. Ratio targets use signed
perpetual position value / equity; identified partial fills conservatively pause
streaming-paper quoting. This is not spot-balance or complete-order parity.

Avellaneda-Stoikov reservation-price/spread design references Hummingbot's
avellaneda_market_making at revision 9af100d6822da7d2d0291a906c730ef172284ee2,
Apache License 2.0. Glyde retains signed perpetual inventory/equity normalization;
the optional book-plus-trade VWAP volatility estimator is a Glyde adaptation,
not Hummingbot's automatic trade-intensity calibration.

The optional glyde_perpetual Hummingbot connector subclasses/adapts Hummingbot's
hyperliquid_perpetual connector at revision
9af100d6822da7d2d0291a906c730ef172284ee2, Apache License 2.0.
Hummingbot contributors retain their upstream copyright. Glyde rewrites the
owner/read-auth/signing boundaries, exact-decimal order wire, metadata precision
and private stream adaptation; the installed upstream framework remains required.
